/T (If an SQL string is built with +, the input can change the meaning of the statement. This is called SQL injection. A ? placeholder sends the value separately, so it is always only data. executemany\(\) prepares the statement once and inserts all the rows, so it is faster than calling execute\(\) again and again. )
/E (If an SQL string is built with +, the input can change the meaning of the statement. This is called SQL injection. A ? placeholder sends the value separately, so it is always only data. executemany\(\) prepares the statement once and inserts all the rows, so it is faster than calling execute\(\) again and again. )
/Pg 39 0 R
/K [17]
>>
